# Restart local Flask after fixes

Owner lesson (**Sep 2026 — anniversary drop %**): code was correct in the tree, but `:5000` still ran an **old** `wsgi` process, so `/api/banner_timeline` returned stale fields (`drop_rate_labels: null`) and `/tl` looked “unfixed.” The owner had to ask why.

Owner lesson (**Oct 2026 — collections disclaimer**): template already had `colDisclaimerTitle`, but Cursor browser preview still showed old `aside#colDisclaimer` with no title. Agent said “hard-refresh” **without restarting Flask** → owner wasted a prompt on stale markup. **That is agent failure, not owner error.**

## Hard rule

After any change that affects the **running local app**, **restart local Flask and verify the response in this same turn** before telling the owner to check `http://127.0.0.1:5000` (or any local path). Do **not** end the turn with “hard-refresh” if Flask still has pre-edit templates/Python.

### Restart when you touched

- `app.py` / `wsgi.py` / imported Python modules (`gasha_official_rates.py`, etc.)
- **Any** `templates/*.html` (Jinja is loaded by the running process — disk edit ≠ what `:5000` serves)
- Master/published data the process loads at boot (or that only refresh after restart)
- Env-dependent server behavior

### Skip restart only when

- Pure client change already verified via hard-refresh (`app.js` → minify + `verify_app_js_bundle.mjs`, CSS with cache bust), **and** no Python/API/**template** change in the same turn
- Local Flask is not running and the owner is only testing Railway/live

## End-of-turn gate (mandatory)

Before the reply that asks the owner to look at local:

1. Restart Flask (script below) if anything in “Restart when you touched” changed.
2. Wait until `Database ready` / `/health` shows `ok` and not booting.
3. **Fetch the path yourself** (`Invoke-WebRequest` / curl) and confirm the new markup or API field is in the bytes (e.g. `colDisclaimerTitle` present). If missing → fix/restart again; do not ping the owner.
4. Only then say they can hard-refresh / re-open the Cursor preview.

Cursor Simple Browser / embedded preview often keeps the previous DOM until the **server** serves new HTML — telling them to refresh while Flask is stale guarantees another wasted prompt.

## How (Windows / this repo)

```powershell
$pids = (Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 5000 -State Listen -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue).OwningProcess | Select-Object -Unique
foreach ($p in $pids) { if ($p -and $p -ne 0) { Stop-Process -Id $p -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue } }
Start-Sleep -Seconds 2
$env:PYTHONIOENCODING='utf-8'
python wsgi.py
```

Run in background; wait until ready; spot-check the fixed path **on local** before saying they can refresh.

## Reply habit

- Say you **restarted local Flask** and **verified** the path when the owner will check `:5000`.
- Do **not** ask them to restart, or leave them debugging stale processes / old markup.
- Still honor `verify-live-before-fixed.mdc` for Railway/live claims.
